      "metadata": {
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "title",
            "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5",
            "text": "OL09-00-005015 - OL 9 must authenticate the remote logging server for offloading audit logs via rsyslog."
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "family": "unix"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "platform",
                "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5",
                "text": "Oracle Linux 9"
              }
            ],
            "name": "affected",
            "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5"
          },
          {
            "name": "description",
            "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5",
            "text": "Information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration.\n\n\tOffloading is a common process in information systems with limited audit storage capacity.\n\n\tOL 9 installation media provides \"rsyslogd\", a system utility providing support for message logging. Support for both internet and Unix domain sockets enables this utility to support both local and remote logging. Coupling this utility with \"gnutls\" (a secure communications library implementing the SSL, TLS, and DTLS protocols) creates a method to securely encrypt and offload auditing.\n\n\t\"Rsyslog\" supported authentication modes include:\n\tanon - anonymous authentication\n\tx509/fingerprint - certificate fingerprint authentication\n\tx509/certvalid - certificate validation only\n\tx509/name - certificate validation and subject name authentication\n\n\tSatisfies: SRG-OS-000342-GPOS-00133, SRG-OS-000479-GPOS-00224"
          }
        ],
        "name": "metadata",
        "namespace": "http://oval.mitre.org/XMLSchema/oval-definitions-5"
      },
      "version": "2"
    }
  ],
